Cherry-picked verbatim from upstream showmycards/showmycards@38c0019b
("feat(backend): ingest Scryfall bulk data as gzipped JSONL", PR #155,
merged 2026-07-20, closes upstream #153). Not in any release tag yet —
v0.3.0 predates it — so we carry it locally. DROP THIS PATCH once
flake.nix pins a tag that contains 38c0019b.

Scryfall retired the plain JSON-array bulk downloads: /bulk-data entries
now expose only `jsonl_download_uri` (+ `compressed_size`), and
`download_uri`/`size` are gone. v0.3.0 read the absent `download_uri`,
got "", and every scheduled refresh died with
  unsupported protocol scheme ""
leaving prices and card details frozen at the last good import.

